WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.690
My sister got a voice message that

2
00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.310
sounded just like her son.

3
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.280
“Mum, I lost my phone, send me money now!”

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.450
But her son was sitting right next to her!

5
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.840
The voice was made by AI.

6
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.810
Today: how AI can make fakes that look and

7
00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.550
sound real, and how you stay safe.

8
00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.270
AI can make pictures of

9
00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.830
things that never happened.

10
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.410
It can copy a person's voice

11
00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.590
from a short recording.

12
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.870
And it can write messages

13
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.330
with perfect spelling.

14
00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:37.490
So looking hard isn't always enough.

15
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.020
Fakes get better every year.

16
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:45.290
What works is a habit: stop, think, ask.

17
00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.220
Stop: don't click, reply or

18
00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.440
send anything yet.

19
00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:54.490
Think: who sent it, and is it rushing me?

20
00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:57.120
Ask: show a grown-up you trust.

21
00:00:58.270 --> 00:00:58.670
Quick check!

22
00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.910
A message says: “You won a new phone!

23
00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.540
Click fast, it ends in ten minutes!”

24
00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:06.650
What's the first thing you do?

25
00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.370
Stop: don't click.

26
00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.530
A rush is a trick to stop you thinking.

27
00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.910
And a prize you never entered

28
00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.550
for is a warning sign.

29
00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.540
Here's a great idea for voices.

30
00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:22.170
Choose a secret code word

31
00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:22.870
with your family.

32
00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.200
If someone calls with a scary

33
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.320
story, ask for the code word.

34
00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.830
A fake voice won't know it!

35
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.820
And never make a fake of a real

36
00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.240
person, even as a joke.

37
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.600
A fake picture can hurt someone badly.

38
00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.600
If you see one of someone you know,

39
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.440
don't share it: tell a grown-up.

40
00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:47.610
In the app, eight messages

41
00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:48.650
arrive on a phone.

42
00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.750
Some are real, and some are scams.

43
00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:54.910
Decide for each one, then

44
00:01:54.910 --> 00:01:56.270
see the warning signs!

45
00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:58.170
Your turn.

46
00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:01.000
You see a funny picture of your

47
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.680
teacher doing something silly.

48
00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.420
It might be made by AI.

49
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.250
What do you do?

50
00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:10.790
Don't share it, and tell a grown-up.

51
00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.690
Remember: AI can make fakes

52
00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.630
that look and sound real.

53
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.770
Stop, think, ask.

54
00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:22.060
And a family code word beats a fake voice.

55
00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:26.410
Try it tomorrow: choose a secret code

56
00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:27.830
word with your family at home.

57
00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:29.960
Don't write it on a phone.

58
00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:33.840
Then practise: if someone calls with a

59
00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.960
scary story, what do you ask?
